<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">The Three Ravens</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">printed <a href="/years/1611">1611</a>; possibly older</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">&quot;The Three Ravens&quot; (Roud 5, Child 26) is an English folk ballad printed in Melismata, a songbook compiled by Thomas Ravenscroft and published in 1611; the song may be older. Three scavenger birds talk over where and what they shall eat. One tells the others of a knight newly slain, but they find him guarded by his loyal hawks and hounds.</p></div>
